          "year": 2002,
          "date_decided": "2002-01-25",
          "holding": "The court held that Neb. Rev. Stat. § 43-283.01 gives a parent no right to demand a separate pre-termination hearing on whether reasonable efforts to preserve and reunify the family were made, and reinstated the termination of parental rights.",
          "relevance": "Section 43-283.01(2), quoted by the court, requires efforts to preserve families before foster placement — the statutory basis for non-court service responses.",
          "quote": "the plain language of § 43-283.01 contains no such directive granting a parent or any other party the right to bring a motion requesting a \"separate hearing\"",
